{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7f3c1a2-4d5e-4f60-9a11-2c3d4e5f6a70",
    "name": "TaskFlow API - Week 1",
    "description": "REST API for the TaskFlow platform (Compu-Vision internship, Week 1).\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Start the backend: `cd backend && npm run dev`\n2. Select this collection and check the `baseUrl` variable (default `http://localhost:5000/api`).\n3. Run **Auth > Register** or **Auth > Login** first. Both save the returned JWT into the `token` collection variable automatically, and every protected request inherits it via collection-level Bearer auth.\n4. **Projects > Create project** saves its id into `projectId`, and **Tasks > Create task** saves `taskId`, so the remaining requests work without copying ids by hand.\n\n## Conventions\n\nSuccess responses are `{ success: true, data: ... }`. Errors are `{ success: false, error: { message, details? } }`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5000/api",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "projectId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "taskId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userEmail",
      "value": "jimmy@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userPassword",
      "value": "Password123",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Reports whether the server is up and whether Mongoose is connected. Returns 503 if the database is unreachable."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns a token', () => pm.expect(body.data.token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.test('does not leak the password', () => pm.expect(body.data.user).to.not.have.property('password'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.data.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Jimmy Abou A\",\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Creates an account and returns a JWT. `role` cannot be set through this endpoint - every new account is a `member`, so nobody can register themselves as an admin. Returns 409 if the email is already taken."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns a token', () => pm.expect(body.data.token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.data.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges email and password for a JWT. A wrong password and an unknown email both return the same 401 message, so the endpoint cannot be used to discover which emails have accounts."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get current user",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('returns the logged-in user', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.user.email).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the user identified by the bearer token. Useful for confirming a token is still valid."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - wrong password (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"DefinitelyWrong1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Protected route without token (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/projects",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["projects"]
            },
            "description": "Demonstrates that the JWT middleware blocks unauthenticated access."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Projects",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create project",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('owner is the current user', () => pm.expect(body.data.owner).to.have.property('name'));",
                  "pm.test('defaults to active', () => pm.expect(body.data.status).to.eql('active'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('projectId', body.data._id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Website Redesign\",\n  \"description\": \"Refresh the public marketing site\",\n  \"status\": \"active\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/projects",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["projects"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a project owned by the authenticated user. `owner` is taken from the token, never from the request body."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List projects",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('is paginated', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().meta).to.have.property('totalPages'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/projects?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["projects"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                },
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "active",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns only projects the caller owns or is a member of. Admins see everything. Supports `page`, `limit` and `status`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get project by id",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('includes its tasks', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.tasks).to.be.an('array'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["projects", "{{projectId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Returns one project with its owner, members and tasks populated. The tasks come from a Mongoose virtual, so they are not duplicated inside the project document."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update project",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('status was updated', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.status).to.eql('on-hold'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"on-hold\",\n  \"description\": \"Paused until the new brand guidelines land\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["projects", "{{projectId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Owner-only. Updatable fields are whitelisted, so `owner` cannot be reassigned by a caller."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create project - invalid status (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('explains which field failed', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.details[0]).to.have.property('field'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Has a valid name\",\n  \"status\": \"banana\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/projects",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["projects"]
            },
            "description": "Shows the validation layer rejecting a value outside the allowed enum, with a per-field explanation."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Tasks",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create task (nested under project)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('defaults to todo', () => pm.expect(body.data.status).to.eql('todo'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('taskId', body.data._id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Design the new homepage\",\n  \"description\": \"Hero, features and footer\",\n  \"priority\": \"high\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/tasks",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["projects", "{{projectId}}", "tasks"]
            },
            "description": "The project id comes from the URL. A task inherits its permissions from its project, so this fails with 403 if you cannot access the project."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create task (flat route)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Set up analytics\",\n  \"project\": \"{{projectId}}\",\n  \"status\": \"in-progress\",\n  \"priority\": \"medium\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks"]
            },
            "description": "Same operation, with the project supplied in the body instead of the path. Both routes are supported because the Week 2 dashboard is more convenient with the flat one."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List tasks",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('returns an array', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data).to.be.an('array'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                },
                {
                  "key": "project",
                  "value": "{{projectId}}",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "todo",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "priority",
                  "value": "high",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns tasks from every project the caller can see. Filterable by `project`, `status`, `priority` and `assignee`. Enable the disabled query params to try them."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List tasks in a project",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/tasks",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["projects", "{{projectId}}", "tasks"]
            },
            "description": "The nested equivalent of `/tasks?project=<id>`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get task by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks", "{{taskId}}"]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update task",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('status is now done', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.status).to.eql('done'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"priority\": \"low\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks", "{{taskId}}"]
            },
            "description": "PATCH rather than PUT, because the client sends only the fields it wants to change. Moving a task to another project requires access to the destination project as well."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update task - invalid status (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"almost-done\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks", "{{taskId}}"]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete task",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks", "{{taskId}}"]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cleanup",
      "description": "Runs last so that a full collection run leaves no test data behind. Deleting the project also deletes any tasks still attached to it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Delete project (cascades tasks)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('reports how many tasks were removed', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data).to.have.property('deletedTasks'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["projects", "{{projectId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Owner-only. MongoDB has no cascading delete, so the API removes the project's remaining tasks itself and reports how many it deleted."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
